# What belongs in this repository, and what does not.
#
# The rule throughout: source is committed, and anything a command can rebuild
# is not. Where that rule costs somebody something, the entry says so rather
# than leaving them to find out after a clone.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Signing material. Never, under any circumstance.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# The upload key is the only thing that proves an update to Google Play came
# from you. Losing it means asking Play to reset it; publishing it means anybody
# can publish as you. The App Store equivalents are the .p8 and .p12 files, and
# the APNs key on the mailbox server is a .p8 too.
android/key.properties
*.jks
*.keystore
*.p8
*.p12
*.pem
*.mobileprovision
*.cer
*.certSigningRequest

# Anything that looks like a secret, wherever it lands.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
secrets.json
service-account*.json
google-services.json
GoogleService-Info.plist

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Build output
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
/build/
.dart_tool/
.flutter-plugins
.flutter-plugins-dependencies
.packages
.pub-cache/
.pub/
/coverage/
*.dill
*.lock.tmp

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The native engine, which is built from the protocol repository
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# `librotelyx_mobile` and the wasm are compiled from `comms-real-e2e`, not
# written here. They are six and a half megabytes of binary that changes on
# every protocol build, which is the worst possible thing to keep in git: every
# version is stored whole, forever, and none of them is readable in a diff.
#
# The cost is that a fresh clone cannot build an APK until they are made. Both
# commands are one line and both are in the repository:
#
#     tool/native/build-android.sh      the three Android ABIs
#     tool/native/build-desktop.sh      this machine
#     tool/dev/build-wasm.sh            the browser
#
# See docs/NATIVE.md.
android/app/src/main/jniLibs/
web/rotelyx/
/macos/Frameworks/librotelyx_mobile.dylib
/windows/native/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Android
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
android/.gradle/
android/captures/
android/local.properties
android/**/GeneratedPluginRegistrant.java
android/app/debug/
android/app/profile/
android/app/release/
*.apk
*.aab
*.ap_
*.dex
*.class

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# iOS
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# `Pods/` is restored by `pod install` from `Podfile.lock`, which *is*
# committed: the lock file is what makes two machines build the same thing.
ios/Pods/
ios/.symlinks/
ios/Flutter/App.framework
ios/Flutter/Flutter.framework
ios/Flutter/Flutter.podspec
ios/Flutter/Generated.xcconfig
ios/Flutter/ephemeral/
ios/Flutter/app.flx
ios/Flutter/app.zip
ios/Flutter/flutter_assets/
ios/ServiceDefinitions.json
ios/Runner/GeneratedPluginRegistrant.*
**/*.xcworkspace/xcuserdata/
**/*.xcodeproj/xcuserdata/
**/*.xcodeproj/project.xcworkspace/xcshareddata/IDEWorkspaceChecks.plist
*.ipa
*.dSYM.zip
*.dSYM

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Desktop
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
linux/flutter/ephemeral/
macos/Flutter/ephemeral/
macos/Flutter/GeneratedPluginRegistrant.swift
macos/Pods/
windows/flutter/ephemeral/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The device captures this session produced
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# `build/shots/` is already covered by /build above and is named here because
# it is the one people look for: hundreds of full-resolution screenshots taken
# while testing the burn animation, the notifications and the camera.
#
# The ones that are *documentation* live in `docs/screens/` and are committed,
# because a document whose images are missing is not a document.
build/shots/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Editors and operating systems
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.idea/
.vscode/
!.vscode/settings.json
*.iml
*.ipr
*.iws
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
*.swp
*~

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Scratch
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
/tmp/
*.log
*.tmp
*.orig
*.rej

# What was deliberately kept
#
#   pubspec.lock          two machines build the same dependency versions
#   ios/Podfile.lock      the same, for CocoaPods
#   assets/               fonts and brand images, which are source
#   docs/screens/         the captures the documentation refers to
#   android/app/build.gradle  including the signing block, which reads a file
#                             that is ignored rather than containing a secret

# Python bytecode from the tools in tool/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
